    "reading-passage": {
      "nodeId": "544:281",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "📖 Reading Passage",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "📖 Reading Passage"
        },
        {
          "text": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Bakery",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Bakery"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Bakery on the Corner\n\nThere is a small bakery on the corner of our street. Every morning, the smell of fresh bread fills the air long before the shop opens at seven.\n\nThe baker, Mr Ahmad, starts work at four in the morning. He mixes flour, water, yeast, and salt to make the dough. After kneading it by hand, he lets it rise for about an hour. Then he shapes the dough into loaves, rolls, and baguettes before placing them in the large oven.\n\nBy the time the first customers arrive, the shelves are full. There are white bread loaves, wholemeal bread, sourdough, and flatbread. On one side of the counter, there are sweet pastries: croissants, Danish pastries, cinnamon rolls, and doughnuts glazed with sugar. The display case also has cakes — chocolate cake, carrot cake, and cheesecake — all made fresh daily.\n\nMr Ahmad's wife manages the front of the shop. She serves customers, wraps orders in paper bags, and operates the till. Regular customers often order birthday cakes or wedding cakes in advance.\n\nThe bakery also sells biscuits, muffins, and scones with jam and cream. On Fridays, they make a special olive bread that sells out within an hour.\n\nI go there every Saturday to buy a loaf of sourdough and two croissants. The bread is always warm, the crust is golden and crunchy, and the inside is soft. Nothing beats fresh bread from a local bakery.",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "The Bakery on the Corner There is a small bakery on the corner of our street. Every morning, the smell of fresh bread fills the air long before the shop opens at seven. The baker, Mr Ahmad, starts work at four in the morning. He mixes flour, water, yeast, and salt to make the dough. After kneading it by hand, he lets it rise for about an hour. Then he shapes the dough into loaves, rolls, and baguettes before placing them in the large oven. By the time the first customers arrive, the shelves are full. There are white bread loaves, wholemeal bread, sourdough, and flatbread. On one side of the counter, there are sweet pastries: croissants, Danish pastries, cinnamon rolls, and doughnuts glazed with sugar. The display case also has cakes — chocolate cake, carrot cake, and cheesecake — all made fresh daily. Mr Ahmad's wife manages the front of the shop. She serves customers, wraps orders in paper bags, and operates the till. Regular customers often order birthday cakes or wedding cakes in advance. The bakery also sells biscuits, muffins, and scones with jam and cream. On Fridays, they make a special olive bread that sells out within an hour. I go there every Saturday to buy a loaf of sourdough and two croissants. The bread is always warm, the crust is golden and crunchy, and the inside is soft. Nothing beats fresh bread from a local bakery."
        },
        {
          "text": "Comprehension Questions",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Comprehension Questions"
        },
        {
          "text": "1. What time does Mr Ahmad start work?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "1. What time does Mr Ahmad start work?"
        },
        {
          "text": "2. What ingredients does he use for the dough?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "2. What ingredients does he use for the dough?"
        },
        {
          "text": "3. What sweet items are on display?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "3. What sweet items are on display?"
        },
        {
          "text": "4. What does Mr Ahmad's wife do in the shop?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "4. What does Mr Ahmad's wife do in the shop?"
        },
        {
          "text": "5. What is special about Fridays at the bakery?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "5. What is special about Fridays at the bakery?"
        }
      ]
    },
